# Nafs Asp deals combat damage to Bot2, who does not pay. Nothing happens on Bot1's turn or in Bot2's upkeep; at the
# beginning of Bot2's draw step - theirs, not the Asp's controller's - the delayed ability triggers (CR 603.7) and Bot2
# loses 1 life, not 1 damage, so the Asp does not trigger again (the rulings). Once that draw step has begun, paying is no
# longer allowed ("before that draw step", CR 116.2c, 500.4), though Bot2's Mox is untapped.
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Nafs Asp
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nafs Asp.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Nafs Asp)
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot2.Life = 19
[T4 Bot2.Draw]
! Bot2.Nafs Asp.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Tapped = false
